Third-party review (2026-08-30)
-------------------------------
The release contains Tapioca's native add-on, Python bridge and package, optional
Grasshopper worker and components, and optional Dynamo runner and ZeroTouch
package. It does not contain an Archicad, Rhino, Grasshopper, Dynamo or .NET
runtime. Those products remain separately installed and licensed.

The native add-on incorporates code from Diligent Engine, cpp-httplib,
MessagePack for C/C++ and nanort. Their source authorities and pinned build inputs
are recorded in AddOn/reference/CATALOG.yaml. The Iconoir notice required for the
compiled palette icons is reproduced in full below.

Other dependency boundaries are:

- The C++ dependencies are downloaded by tools/build/provision-reference.ps1 from
  the authorities recorded in AddOn/reference/CATALOG.yaml. Neither the Archicad
  Development Kit nor any other SDK is committed here, and no Graphisoft header
  text appears in these sources.
- NotebookUI declares no runtime dependencies. Its build-time tooling
  (TypeScript, Vite, vite-plugin-singlefile) is installed by npm from the
  versions pinned in AddOn/EvP/NotebookUI/package-lock.json; consult that
  lockfile and the upstream package metadata before redistributing a built
  bundle.
- The Tapir command schema (ENZYME-APD/tapir-archicad-automation) is used during
  development only and is deliberately excluded from this repository. Fetch it
  from its own project if you need it.
- Tapioca.GhWorker and Tapioca.Grasshopper are compiled by the .NET SDK against
  NuGet packages pinned in their .csproj files: Rhino.Inside (McNeel, MIT),
  RhinoCommon and Grasshopper (McNeel, under Rhino's own licence). The release
  includes Rhino.Inside.dll. RhinoCommon and Grasshopper are compile-time-only
  references and are not copied or redistributed; the assemblies that run come
  from the user's separately installed and licensed Rhino 8.
- Tapioca.Dynamo and Tapioca.DynamoRunner are compiled against Dynamo Core 4.2.1.
  The release includes only Tapioca's assemblies, package manifest, customization
  file and example graph. It does not include Dynamo Core or Autodesk binaries.
  The user supplies the separately licensed Dynamo runtime, either through
  TAPIOCA_DYNAMO_DIR or in the documented directory beside the add-on. Dynamo
  Core is available from the DynamoDS/Dynamo project under Apache-2.0.

Notable upstream components used by the build, each under its own license:

- Graphisoft Archicad API Development Kit
- Diligent Engine
- cpp-httplib
- MessagePack for C/C++
- nanort
- GoogleTest
- CPython
- Rhino.Inside, RhinoCommon and Grasshopper (McNeel)
- Dynamo Core (DynamoDS/Autodesk)

